/* R12 — LN PO_Update contract. This expression IS the wire body: R12/D13 deleted the compiled C# PO
   payload builders, so nothing else contributes to the request.

   All three PO_Update expressions (PoAccept / PoReject / PoNegotiationApprove) are this same text with a
   different POStatus literal — keep them that way, it is what makes a correction a three-file find/replace.

   Dates arrive pre-formatted from the input-document builder as ISO-8601 seconds-precision UTC with an
   explicit Z. Verified 2026-07-29: LN echoes that form back unchanged, whereas a zone-less value is
   silently defaulted to UTC-05:00.

   D7 — PlannedDeliveryDate / ConfirmedReceiptDate carry the one date every line agrees on; headerDeliveryDate
   is null when they disagree or any line has none, and `x != null ? x` then omits the key.
   !! Omitting these keys makes LN echo the literal string "[object Object]" and still answer Status:"Success"
   (probe run 3, 2026-07-29). Whether it PERSISTS that garbage is unconfirmed. If probe P8a/P8b shows that an
   explicit null or "" is handled cleanly, switch the two lines below — that is a config edit, no deploy.

   D6 — only lines carrying a delivery date go on the wire; the input document deliberately supplies ALL
   non-deleted lines (D24) so this filter is the single place the decision lives. If probe P5a shows LN CLOSES
   a line omitted from Lines[], delete the `[deliveryDate != null]` predicate and the whole line set ships.

   The [ ... ] around the Lines mapping is mandatory (D-R9-13): without it JSONata collapses a single-element
   result to a bare object. It also yields [] for a PO with no dated lines, which is D8. */
{
    "PurchaseOrderDetail": {
        "CompanyCode": companyCode,
        "OrderNo": poNumber,
        "PlannedDeliveryDate": headerDeliveryDate != null ? headerDeliveryDate,
        "ConfirmedReceiptDate": headerDeliveryDate != null ? headerDeliveryDate,
        "POStatus": "Accepted",
        "Lines": [lines[deliveryDate != null].{
            "LineNo": $string(positionNo),
            "SeqNo": $string(sequenceNo),
            "PlannedDeliveryDate": deliveryDate
        }]
    }
}
